        <briefdescription>
<para>This function sends an IPI request to get the XilOcp library version and capability bits running on the PLM. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>- Pointer to the client instance </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>LibInfo</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>- Pointer to Xil_LibInfo. LibVersion and Capability are filled on success. The Version and NistStatus fields are reserved for XilOcp and must be ignored.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS - If the library information is read successfully</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_INVALID_PARAM - If any input parameter is invalid</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE - On failure </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Performs input parameter validation.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Query library info via the Features command using a valid OCP api-id as the selector, so the command succeeds and the server returns the library version/capability at fixed indices.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Sends the request to the server and copies the IPI payload after the status word.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>        </inbodydescription>
